@startuml "Facade - Transcode (Homework) - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Facade — homework 3, where the knowledge is the order


class VideoConverter <<Facade>> {
  + convert(source, target)
}

class Demuxer
class AudioDecoder
class VideoDecoder
class Scaler
class Encoder
class Muxer

VideoConverter ..> Demuxer
VideoConverter ..> AudioDecoder
VideoConverter ..> VideoDecoder
VideoConverter ..> Scaler
VideoConverter ..> Encoder
VideoConverter ..> Muxer

note right of VideoConverter
  demux -> decode -> scale
  -> encode -> mux
end note

note as N1
  Six classes, each easy on its own.

  They work in <b>one order</b>, and nothing in
  their interfaces says so. Get it wrong and
  there is no error — just a file that is
  quietly wrong.

  That is the most valuable thing a facade
  can absorb: knowledge a client could not
  have discovered from the subsystem itself.
end note

@enduml
